    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "I'm thinking that this may be possible by taking a slice of dynamic shared memory and reshaping it, once #5099 is merged to fix #5073 (at the moment slicing dynamic shared memory doesn't really work properly). So perhaps once could do something like:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n@cuda.jit\r\ndef matrix_multiplies(r, A, x, n_matrices):\r\n    dynsmem = cuda.shared.array(0, dtype=float32)\r\n    matrices = dynsmem[:n_matrices * 4].reshape(n_matrices, 2, 2)\r\n    for i in range(n_matrices):\r\n        # Do something with each 2x2 matrix in dynamic shared memory\r\n    # ...\r\n```\r\n\r\nI haven't tried this yet, but I think it might be a way to have 2D+ dynamic shared arrays.",
