    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "It turns out that my strategy above does not work because reshaping shared arrays does not work:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom numba import cuda, types\r\n\r\n\r\n@cuda.jit\r\ndef foo():\r\n    a_cache = cuda.shared.array((32, 32), types.int32)\r\n    a_cache.reshape(64, 16)\r\n\r\n\r\nfoo[1, 1]()\r\n```\r\n\r\ngives:\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ python noreshape.py \r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/home/nfs/gmarkall/numbadev/numba/numba/cuda/cudadrv/driver.py\", line 1711, in complete\r\n    driver.cuLinkComplete(self.handle, byref(cubin), byref(size))\r\n  File \"/home/nfs/gmarkall/numbadev/numba/numba/cuda/cudadrv/driver.py\", line 294, in safe_cuda_api_call\r\n    self._check_error(fname, retcode)\r\n  File \"/home/nfs/gmarkall/numbadev/numba/numba/cuda/cudadrv/driver.py\", line 329, in _check_error\r\n    raise CudaAPIError(retcode, msg)\r\nnumba.cuda.cudadrv.driver.CudaAPIError: [999] Call to cuLinkComplete results in CUDA_ERROR_UNKNOWN\r\n\r\nDuring handling of the above exception, another exception occurred:\r\n\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"noreshape.py\", line 10, in <module>\r\n    foo[1, 1]()\r\n  File \"/home/nfs/gmarkall/numbadev/numba/numba/cuda/compiler.py\", line 804, in __call__\r\n    kernel = self.specialize(*args)\r\n  File \"/home/nfs/gmarkall/numbadev/numba/numba/cuda/compiler.py\", line 815, in specialize\r\n    kernel = self.compile(argtypes)\r\n  File \"/home/nfs/gmarkall/numbadev/numba/numba/cuda/compiler.py\", line 834, in compile\r\n    kernel.bind()\r\n  File \"/home/nfs/gmarkall/numbadev/numba/numba/cuda/compiler.py\", line 548, in bind\r\n    self._func.get()\r\n  File \"/home/nfs/gmarkall/numbadev/numba/numba/cuda/compiler.py\", line 433, in get\r\n    cubin, _size = linker.complete()\r\n  File \"/home/nfs/gmarkall/numbadev/numba/numba/cuda/cudadrv/driver.py\", line 1713, in complete\r\n    raise LinkerError(\"%s\\n%s\" % (e, self.error_log))\r\nnumba.cuda.cudadrv.driver.LinkerError: [999] Call to cuLinkComplete results in CUDA_ERROR_UNKNOWN\r\nerror   : Undefined reference to 'numba_attempt_nocopy_reshape' in '<cudapy-ptx>'\r\n```\r\n\r\n(above example without dynamic shared memory for simplicity, but dynamic shared memory has the same problem)",
